      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · \"Once Upon a Time\" and \"Fall Out\" (paraphrased); Barr's episode studies; BFI's qualification",
          "title": "Degree Absolute; the masks; the escape",
          "italic": "The finale turns the sovereign position inward without cancelling the material apparatus: removal from one setting does not establish that the desire to monopolise the deciding position has ended.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "In \"Once Upon a Time\" the Two of \"The Chimes of Big Ben\" returns and commits to Degree Absolute: a week of isolation in the embryo room, working through regression, nursery language, counting and enacted stages of life. The struggle reverses; Six gains the upper hand and Two dies as the period ends; the Supervisor arrives and Six demands to see Number One. \"Fall Out\" brings Six before a masked assembly and its President: his resistance acclaimed as qualifying him for freedom and possibly leadership; Two resuscitated; Two and the younger Number Forty-Eight appear",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "as forms of revolt to be judged while Six is ceremonially distinguished. Invited to speak, his first-person address is drowned out. Beneath One's outer mask is an ape mask; beneath that, a face identical to his own. Six starts a rocket countdown, frees Two and Forty-Eight, and escapes with them and the Butler. The escapees travel toward London; Forty-Eight goes his own way; Two enters Parliament; the Butler accompanies Six home — where the door opens automatically, recalling the Village. BFI qualifies any claim that London supplies an unequivocal final exterior.\n\nOccurrences: the embryo room week (#2); the masks and the own face (#2); the countdown and rescue (#2); the automatic door and closing drive (#2, returned at #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
