      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#5→0 · Q27 political return; A30/C42; C57; A32; M02, M20, M24, M26, M40, M46, M48",
          "title": "Return without inheriting the hidden throne",
          "italic": "The whole demonstrates the exact consequence: release must reach the office of measure as well as its current occupant — a larger shared account gains no exemption from the question asked of the smaller one.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Six leaves the Village with others; the last movement retains the Butler, Forty-Eight and the former Two alongside him, then follows their divergence. The familiar face beneath One's masks and the automatic door in London alter the sense of arrival without making every act of escape fictitious. Q27's political return grounds the consequence: a counter-position must be able to return the field rather than take possession of the office it opposed. A30/C42 define a shared world where actions change others' conditions with grounds remaining distinct — the Village as counter-image of shared conditions administered without reciprocity. C57 extends the",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "question to persistent artifacts, permissions and inherited accounts; A32 demands the reply be able to revise the image, its measure and the institution holding it. The whole returns-to M02 through subject and assigned predicate, M20 through a cut whose apparatus and authority stay visible, M40 through the hidden evaluator — repeating the subject's score reproduces Two's deflection — M46 with governed participants able to contest the counting operation, and M48 through a federation answerable to sources and consequence. Rover, the embryo room, Fifty-Eight and the rocket receive no symbolic equation to a native determination (human-amplified: no).\n\nOccurrences: the divergence of the escapees (#2, #5→0); the automatic door (#2, #5→0); the contested count (#0, #3, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
